# ABP Layered Application Template

> **Docs**: https://abp.io/docs/latest/solution-templates/layered-web-application

CoachApp is a **single-application** ABP 10.4.0 / .NET 10 solution. It keeps the classic
DDD **layer projects** but organizes each layer by **feature folder**. There is **no
`modules/` folder** — everything lives under `src/`. The `Trainee` / `TrainingPlan` slices
are the reference; mirror them file-for-file.

## Solution Structure

```
CoachApp/
├── src/
│   ├── CoachApp.Domain.Shared/            # Consts, enums, error codes, localization
│   │   ├── Entites/<Feature>/             #   <Entity>Consts.cs
│   │   ├── Enums/                         #   <Enum>.cs  (namespace CoachApp.Enums)
│   │   ├── Localization/CoachApp/         #   en.json, ar.json
│   │   └── CoachAppDomainErrorCodes.cs
│   ├── CoachApp.Domain/                   # Entities / aggregate roots
│   │   └── Entites/<Feature>/             #   <Entity>.cs  (+ <Entity>Manager only if truly needed)
│   ├── CoachApp.Application.Contracts/    # DTOs, service interfaces, permissions
│   │   ├── Entites/<Feature>/             #   <Entity>Dto, CreateUpdate<Entity>Dto, Get<Entity>ListInput, I<Entity>AppService
│   │   └── Permissions/                   #   CoachAppPermissions, CoachAppPermissionDefinitionProvider
│   ├── CoachApp.Application/              # Application service implementations
│   │   ├── Apis/<Feature>/               #   <Entity>AppService.cs
│   │   ├── CoachAppMapsterConfig.cs      #   central Mapster mapping config
│   │   └── MapsterObjectMapper.cs
│   ├── CoachApp.EntityFrameworkCore/     # Single DbContext + per-feature EF config + migrations
│   │   ├── EntityFrameworkCore/          #   CoachAppDbContext.cs
│   │   ├── EntityConfigurations/<Feature>/  # <Entity>Configuration : IEntityTypeConfiguration<T>
│   │   └── Migrations/
│   ├── CoachApp.HttpApi.Host/            # Host: conventional (auto) controllers, Swagger
│   └── CoachApp.DbMigrator/              # Applies migrations + seeds data
└── test/
    ├── CoachApp.Domain.Tests/
    ├── CoachApp.Application.Tests/
    └── CoachApp.EntityFrameworkCore.Tests/
```

## Layer Responsibilities

| Layer | Responsibility | References |
|-------|---------------|------------|
| **Domain.Shared** | Consts, enums, error codes, localization keys | Nothing |
| **Domain** | Entities / aggregate roots; `*Manager` only for a genuine cross-aggregate rule | Domain.Shared |
| **Application.Contracts** | DTOs, `I<Entity>AppService`, permissions | Domain.Shared |
| **Application** | AppService orchestration + querying, Mapster config | Domain, Application.Contracts |
| **EntityFrameworkCore** | Single `CoachAppDbContext`, `IEntityTypeConfiguration<T>`, migrations | Domain |
| **HttpApi.Host** | Conventional controllers (auto-exposed app services), host wiring | Application.Contracts |
| **DbMigrator** | Database migration + seeding console app | EntityFrameworkCore |

## Feature-based namespaces (layer name dropped)

| Concern | Project → folder | Namespace |
|---|---|---|
| Entity (+ optional Manager) | `Domain` → `Entites/<Feature>/` | `CoachApp.Entites.<Feature>` |
| Consts | `Domain.Shared` → `Entites/<Feature>/` | `CoachApp.Entites.<Feature>` |
| Enums | `Domain.Shared` → `Enums/` | `CoachApp.Enums` |
| Error codes | `Domain.Shared` (root) | `CoachApp` |
| DTOs + `I<Entity>AppService` | `Application.Contracts` → `Entites/<Feature>/` | `CoachApp.Entites.<Feature>` |
| Permissions | `Application.Contracts` → `Permissions/` | `CoachApp.Permissions` |
| AppService | `Application` → `Apis/<Feature>/` | `CoachApp.Apis.<Feature>` |
| Mapster config | `Application` (root) | `CoachApp` |
| EF configuration | `EntityFrameworkCore` → `EntityConfigurations/<Feature>/` | `CoachApp.EntityConfigurations.<Feature>` |

`<Feature>` is the pluralized entity (`Trainees`, `TrainingPlans`).

## Adding a New Feature

### 1. Constants + enum in Domain.Shared
```csharp
// Entites/Trainees/TraineeConsts.cs  (namespace CoachApp.Entites.Trainees)
public static class TraineeConsts
{
    public const int MaxCodeLength = 32;
    public const int MaxFirstNameLength = 64;
    public const int MaxLastNameLength = 64;
}

// Enums/Gender.cs  (namespace CoachApp.Enums) — byte-backed, explicit values
public enum Gender : byte { Unspecified = 0, Male = 1, Female = 2 }

// CoachAppDomainErrorCodes.cs — one code per business rule
public const string TraineeCodeAlreadyExists = "CoachApp:00001";
```

### 2. Entity in Domain (pragmatic — public setters + static Create)
```csharp
// Entites/Trainees/Trainee.cs  (namespace CoachApp.Entites.Trainees)
public class Trainee : FullAuditedAggregateRoot<Guid>, IMultiTenant
{
    public virtual Guid? TenantId { get; set; }
    public virtual string Code { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public virtual string FirstName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public virtual bool IsActive { get; set; }

    protected Trainee() { } // For ORM

    public static Trainee Create(Guid id, string code, string firstName, Guid? tenantId = null)
    {
        return new Trainee
        {
            Id = id,
            Code = Check.NotNullOrWhiteSpace(code, nameof(code), TraineeConsts.MaxCodeLength),
            FirstName = Check.NotNullOrWhiteSpace(firstName, nameof(firstName), TraineeConsts.MaxFirstNameLength),
            TenantId = tenantId,
            IsActive = true
        };
    }
}
```
Guard a **real invariant** (one that needs no I/O) with a behavior method that throws and keep
its fields `protected set` — e.g. `TrainingPlan.SetSchedule(start, end)` enforcing `end > start`.
Do **not** add a `*Factory`; add a `*Manager` only for a genuine cross-aggregate rule.

### 3. DTOs + service interface in Application.Contracts
```csharp
// Entites/Trainees/TraineeDto.cs
public class TraineeDto : FullAuditedEntityDto<Guid>
{
    public string Code { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string FirstName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public bool IsActive { get; set; }
}

// Entites/Trainees/CreateUpdateTraineeDto.cs — DataAnnotations validation
public class CreateUpdateTraineeDto
{
    [Required, StringLength(TraineeConsts.MaxCodeLength)]
    public string Code { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Required, StringLength(TraineeConsts.MaxFirstNameLength)]
    public string FirstName { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    public bool IsActive { get; set; } = true;
}

// Entites/Trainees/GetTraineeListInput.cs
public class GetTraineeListInput : PagedAndSortedResultRequestDto
{
    public string? Filter { get; set; }
    public bool? IsActive { get; set; }
}

// Entites/Trainees/ITraineeAppService.cs — Id passed separately from the update DTO
public interface ITraineeAppService : IApplicationService
{
    Task<TraineeDto> GetAsync(Guid id);
    Task<PagedResultDto<TraineeDto>> GetListAsync(GetTraineeListInput input);
    Task<TraineeDto> CreateAsync(CreateUpdateTraineeDto input);
    Task<TraineeDto> UpdateAsync(Guid id, CreateUpdateTraineeDto input);
    Task DeleteAsync(Guid id);
}
```

### 4. Permissions in Application.Contracts
```csharp
// Permissions/CoachAppPermissions.cs
public static class CoachAppPermissions
{
    public const string GroupName = "CoachApp";

    public static class Trainees
    {
        public const string Default = GroupName + ".Trainees";
        public const string Create = Default + ".Create";
        public const string Update = Default + ".Update";
        public const string Delete = Default + ".Delete";
    }
}
// Register the children in CoachAppPermissionDefinitionProvider.Define(...).
```

### 5. Fat AppService in Application (generic repository, inline querying)
```csharp
// Apis/Trainees/TraineeAppService.cs  (namespace CoachApp.Apis.Trainees)
[Authorize(CoachAppPermissions.Trainees.Default)]
public class TraineeAppService : CoachAppAppService, ITraineeAppService
{
    private readonly IRepository<Trainee, Guid> _traineeRepository;

    public TraineeAppService(IRepository<Trainee, Guid> traineeRepository)
        => _traineeRepository = traineeRepository;

    public virtual async Task<PagedResultDto<TraineeDto>> GetListAsync(GetTraineeListInput input)
    {
        var query = await _traineeRepository.GetQueryableAsync();
        query = query
            .WhereIf(!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(input.Filter), x => x.Code.Contains(input.Filter!))
            .WhereIf(input.IsActive.HasValue, x => x.IsActive == input.IsActive!.Value);

        var totalCount = await AsyncExecuter.CountAsync(query);
        var sorting = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(input.Sorting) ? $"{nameof(Trainee.Code)} asc" : input.Sorting;
        var trainees = await AsyncExecuter.ToListAsync(
            query.OrderBy(sorting).Skip(input.SkipCount).Take(input.MaxResultCount));

        return new PagedResultDto<TraineeDto>(
            totalCount, ObjectMapper.Map<List<Trainee>, List<TraineeDto>>(trainees));
    }

    [Authorize(CoachAppPermissions.Trainees.Create)]
    public virtual async Task<TraineeDto> CreateAsync(CreateUpdateTraineeDto input)
    {
        await CheckCodeDuplicationAsync(input.Code); // cross-aggregate rule that needs the repo
        var trainee = Trainee.Create(GuidGenerator.Create(), input.Code, input.FirstName, CurrentTenant.Id);
        await _traineeRepository.InsertAsync(trainee, autoSave: true);
        return ObjectMapper.Map<Trainee, TraineeDto>(trainee);
    }
}
```

### 6. Mapster mapping line in Application
```csharp
// CoachAppMapsterConfig.Configure() — entity → DTO only, grouped by feature
TypeAdapterConfig<Trainee, TraineeDto>.NewConfig();
```

### 7. EF configuration + DbSet in EntityFrameworkCore
```csharp
// EntityConfigurations/Trainees/TraineeConfiguration.cs
public class TraineeConfiguration : IEntityTypeConfiguration<Trainee>
{
    public void Configure(EntityTypeBuilder<Trainee> b)
    {
        b.ToTable(CoachAppConsts.DbTablePrefix + "Trainees", CoachAppConsts.DbSchema);
        b.ConfigureByConvention();
        b.Property(x => x.Code).IsRequired().HasMaxLength(TraineeConsts.MaxCodeLength);
        b.Property(x => x.Gender).HasConversion<byte>();
        b.HasIndex(x => new { x.TenantId, x.Code });
    }
}
// Auto-applied by builder.ApplyConfigurationsFromAssembly(...) — you just add the class.

// CoachAppDbContext.cs — one DbSet per aggregate on the single DbContext
public DbSet<Trainee> Trainees { get; set; }
```

### 8. Localization
Add keys to **both** `Domain.Shared/Localization/CoachApp/en.json` and `ar.json`
(`Permission:Trainees` + `.Create/.Update/.Delete`, the `CoachApp:0000N` message, field labels).

### 9. Migration (write freely — ASK before applying)
```bash
dotnet ef migrations add Added_Trainee \
  --project src/CoachApp.EntityFrameworkCore \
  --startup-project src/CoachApp.EntityFrameworkCore

# Apply ONLY with the user's approval (also seeds):
dotnet run --project src/CoachApp.DbMigrator
```

## DbMigrator

Console application for applying database migrations and seeding initial data (admin user,
permissions, etc.). Run it (with approval) before first launch.

## Best Practices

1. **Respect layer boundaries** — never reference EntityFrameworkCore from Application.
2. **Pragmatic domain** — public setters + `static Create`; invariants as behavior methods; no default Factory/Manager.
3. **Generic repository for CRUD** — `IRepository<T, Guid>`; custom repo only for a complex, reused query.
4. **Fat AppService** — orchestration + inline querying + cross-aggregate checks live here.
5. **DTOs at boundaries** — never expose entities; map entity → DTO via `ObjectMapper` (Mapster).
6. **Conventional controllers** — ABP auto-exposes app services; don't hand-write controllers.
7. **Mapster for mapping** — central `CoachAppMapsterConfig`, not Mapperly/AutoMapper.
8. **Migrations are the schema** — write them freely, but ASK before applying.
